                  %use{:x => "71.666923", "xlink:href" => "#WTY4oedsQkHvYKfU-taHXw4onDA=-glyph3-1", :y => "39.296475"}
            %p
          This is due to
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#EilenbergMoore65"} Eilenberg &amp; Moore 1965
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk92"} MacLane &amp; Moerdijk 1992, Thm. 2 on p. 249
          %h3#general_adjoint_coalgebras_
            General adjoint (co)algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End(A)
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor+category"} endofunctor category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End(A)
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctors"} endofunctors
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            between them, with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+composition"} vertical composition
            as
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            with respect to the composition as the tensor product of objects (endofunctor) and Godement product (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"}> horizontal composition
            ) as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            of morphisms (natural transformations). Hence we can consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+operads"} algebras over operads
          %p
            In any case, given an adjunction
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\dashv G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^n\to T
            dualize to cooperations
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\to G^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^k\to T^l
            dualize to the multioperations
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mi l
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^l\to G^k
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            (and more generally there is a duality among the identities for multioperations). This is essentially the consequence of
          %p
            %strong Lemma.
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+%C5%A0koda"}> Zoran
            ) Given the adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\dashv G
            with unit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            and counit
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mi k
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi α
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mi l
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi β
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  T^k \stackrel{\alpha}\longrightarrow T^l\stackrel\beta\longrightarrow T^s
          %p
            the composition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi α
                    %mo *
                  %mo ∘
                  %msup
                    %mi β
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha^*\circ\beta^*
            of the dual (in the above sense) sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mi k
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟵
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi α
                        %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mi l
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟵
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi β
                        %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G^k \stackrel{\alpha^*}\longleftarrow G^l\stackrel{\beta^*}\longleftarrow G^s
          %p
            equal to the dual
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi β
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi α
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\beta\circ\alpha)^*
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta\circ\alpha
          %p
            %em> Proof
            \.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
            notices that this is a special case of known contravariant functoriality of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mate"} mate
          %p We need to prove that the composition
          .maruku-equation
