          %h2#examples_2 Examples
          %h3#adjoint_modalities Adjoint modalities
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+modality"} adjoint modality
            is an example of a pair of adjoint monads.
          %h2#references References
          %p Discussion of adjoint monads originates with
          %ul
            %li#EilenbergMoore65
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Eilenberg"}> Samuel Eilenberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Moore"} John Moore
              = succeed "," do
                %em Adjoint functors and triples
              %strong 9
              3 (1965) 381-398 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1215/ijm/1256068141"}> doi:10.1215/ijm/1256068141
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            (there called “adjoint triples”, sticking with the old term “triple” for “monad”, a terminology that now clashes with the modern use of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triples"} adjoint triples
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li#MacLaneMoerdijk92
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+Mac+Lane"}> Saunders Mac Lane
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic — A First Introduction to Topos Theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-0927-0"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4612-0927-0
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ambidextrous+adjunctions"} ambidextrous adjunctions
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+monads"} Frobenius monads
          %ul
            %li#Street04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Frobenius monads and pseudomonoids
                %strong 45
                3930 (2004) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1788852"}> doi:10.1063/1.1788852
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Lauda05
